readme=f'''# Lobby2 mission framework cleanup

Commit: {commit}. Installed and pushed to codex/game-master-playable.

Flags are optional. Regular GC_Event and Random Event Group types, a Game Mode State condition, a Group Condition (All/Any/None/Not all) and separate Count Condition (Greater than/Less than/Equal/Not equal), both with nested children, Advanced Random Chance (0..1, default 1), distinct eligible-child selection, and optional initial flags. The separate Event selector is removed. State conditions use the existing game-mode callback; Scheduled Random Chance conditions provide a configurable interval, 0..1 chance, and a Roll Once checkbox. Two-choice framework settings use named boolean checkboxes, with true/false terminology; Start Call Count defaults to zero (false); a positive starting count remembers prior calls and means true. One or more calls remains true, including for repeatable flags. Reset Flag clears the count and rearms activation. Nested logical groups combine their cached answers normally. Casualties provides an integrated faction filter, Players/AI/Both selector and a fixed match-start casualty ratio. Total Deaths uses the same filters with count comparisons and includes respawned lives. Entity Damage observes a named existing character, vehicle or destructible object through its shared damage manager, with Destroyed, Not destroyed or Damage amount and an optional named damage area. One Area Condition references either RadiusArea or PolygonArea; one-second server sampling caches names, geometry and target selections, uses squared distance or the engine polygon test, and publishes result changes. Area Condition supports Named Entities or Players / AI, with optional faction filters and Count or living-character Proportion requirements. Living Characters is a general living-population count without area settings. Proportion measures eligible living characters on one side against the total living population; no eligible characters means false. Both conditions share the existing sampler. Previous area-based Living Characters setups require migration to Area Condition; legacy area Counts remain readable. Type/prefab discovery remains deferred; no vehicle lifecycle hooks or world scans were added. A reusable Mission Interaction component/action and empty Interaction prefab support native action contexts, optional faction/flag gates, an output flag call, and a temporary Interaction Condition signal. Signals reset after the notification chain even when other conditions fail; events own repetition and flags own persistent memory. Interaction input, prefab instantiation and network behavior remain untested in Play. General timer conditions remain a future slice. Advanced event settings are direct fields in an Advanced category shared by regular events and random groups; old GC_RuleOptions wrappers require flattening as documented. Workbench owns category expansion; no default-collapse API is exposed. Mission Events, Mission Flags, briefing and parameters stay together at the top of GC_LobbyManager.

The standard-logic slice passed 560 checks before the final ordering correction in Workbench 1.9.0.37 embedded Play. Source received independent review. The final ordering correction compiled and received source-level logic review; three new ordering regressions were not run in-game at the user's request. Nested logic and serialized state examples passed live tests. Real Lobby2 phase transitions, duplicate notification handling, unauthenticated rejection and engine stop were also checked. Fixed Boolean authoring placeholders were removed; fixed test inputs exist only in the optional test scripts. Full object-class picker options are not independently verified. Mission Flag Condition, Mission Event Condition and the combined Count Condition now support remembered calls, conditions and explicit flag reset (mission event pulses remain temporary); live entity numeric sources remain deferred. Known unrelated Arland GUID/menu-preset diagnostics remain. Scheduled random conditions received production script compilation and source-level review only; their new optional regression scenarios were not run in-game. Entity Damage now dispatches registered native damage callbacks immediately on condition-answer changes, without shared-tick damage polling. It received production script compilation and independent source-level logic/lifecycle review; no in-game damage tests were run. Area Condition and its passive shape prefabs received script compilation and independent source review; gameplay, preview appearance and benchmarks were not run. Dedicated/remote-client behavior was not newly tested.

Read docs/MissionRules/README.md for setup, examples and compatibility. This is a source update for the existing Lobby2 project, not a standalone addon.

The saved schema changed. Existing project examples were migrated, but external older rules need conversion. When installing these snapshot files, remove obsolete scripts/Game/MissionFramework/GC_MissionEvent.c, GC_MissionRule.c, GC_MissionCondition.c, GC_RuleDefinition.c and GC_SimpleMissionRule.c (and GC_MissionRulesComponent.c from the earliest package). Preserve your other authored files. The included cleanup.patch records the complete changes, including deletions, against 29df833.

Optional tests require the existing MCP test addon. This package uses committed source and excludes unrelated local scene edits. The current local example layer retains the user's edits, including empty rule entries converted to the canonical Mission Event configuration.
'''
target=out/'Lobby2-MissionFramework-Cleanup.zip'
with zipfile.ZipFile(io.BytesIO(archive)) as src, zipfile.ZipFile(target,'w',zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED) as dst:
 for name in src.namelist():
  if not name.endswith('/'): dst.writestr(name,src.read(name))
 dst.writestr('README.md',readme)
 dst.writestr('cleanup.patch',git('diff','29df833','HEAD','--binary'))
with zipfile.ZipFile(target) as z:
 assert z.testzip() is None
 assert not any(n.endswith(('GC_MissionEvent.c','GC_MissionRule.c','GC_MissionCondition.c','GC_RuleDefinition.c','GC_SimpleMissionRule.c')) for n in z.namelist())
 for name in ['tests/McpTestAddon/scripts/Game/GC_LegacyRuleFixture.c','tests/McpTestAddon/scripts/Game/GC_StandardLogicTests.c','tests/McpTestAddon/scripts/Game/GC_GameModeConditionTests.c','tests/McpTestAddon/scripts/Game/GC_EventGroupTests.c','tests/McpTestAddon/scripts/Game/GC_FlagMemoryTests.c','tests/McpTestAddon/Prefabs/FlagMemoryExample.et','tests/McpTestAddon/Prefabs/FlagMemoryExample.et.meta',
'tests/McpTestAddon/worlds/StandardLogicExample.ent','tests/McpTestAddon/worlds/StandardLogicExample.ent.meta','tests/McpTestAddon/worlds/StandardLogicExample_Layers/default.layer','tests/McpTestAddon/scripts/Game/GC_MissionRandomTests.c','tests/McpTestAddon/scripts/Game/GC_RandomConditionTests.c','tests/McpTestAddon/scripts/Game/GC_CasualtyConditionTests.c']:
  assert name in z.namelist()
(out/'MissionFramework-README.md').write_bytes(git('show','HEAD:docs/MissionRules/README.md'))
print(f'Package verified: {target.name}; {len(zipfile.ZipFile(target).namelist())} files; commit {commit[:7]}')
